/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An RC tree has one input (the driver) and resistors that branch out without loops, with a capacitor from every node to ground.
   - τDi = Σk CkRik Here the sum runs over every capacitor Ck in the tree, including those on side branches.
   - Mathematically τDi is the first moment of the node's impulse response, the average arrival time of its edge.
   - For an RC ladder (a chain) the rule becomes: each capacitor is multiplied by all the resistance between it and the driver.
   - R and C are the totals of the line.
   - So the Elmore delay of a distributed wire is RC/2, against the exact 50% delay of 0.38RC.
   - A conducting transistor is a resistor, and every internal node of a stack has diffusion capacitance.
   - This gives two design rules.
*/
