/* book Worked example 2: Q: To gain speed, the same block is moved to transistors whose threshold is 100 mV lower. The subthreshold swing is S = 100 mV per decade and subthreshold current dominates the leakage. Find the new leakage power and the new crossover frequency.
   1. A 100 mV drop in Vt with S = 100 mV/decade raises the subthreshold current by 10100/100 = 10 times: 10 µA → 100 µA.
   2. Pleak = 1.8 V × 100 µA = 180 µW.
   3. Crossover = 100 × 10⁻⁶/(0.1 × 50 × 10⁻¹² × 1.8) = 11.1 MHz.
   4. At 100 MHz the total becomes 1.62 + 0.18 = 1.80 mW, 10% more for the same work.
   Answer: Leakage rises tenfold to 180 µW and the crossover moves up to 11.1 MHz. */
